{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 518886, "name": "Natha TERR", "username": "njxt72", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/n/3c6eb4/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-07-23T07:05:11.899Z", "cooked": "<p>Here’s my hardware :</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>CPU : AMD Ryzen 7 7800X3D</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>MB : MSI X870 GAMING PLUS WIFI</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>RAM : G.Skill RipJaws S5 Low Profile 32 Go (2 x 16 Go) DDR5 6600 MHz CL34</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>SSD :    1. Kingston SSD NV3 2 To     2. Kingston SSD NV3 1 To</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>GPU : ASUS TUF Gaming GeForce RTX 4070 SUPER OC Edition 12 GB</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>GPU Driver : proprietary Nvidia 610.x</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Screen : LG 27\" LED - UltraGear en displayport</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Fedora (KDE) 43 then 44 was working fine for months, I was doing all the updates almost immediately as they were available.</p>\n<p>The latest one (with the kernel 7.1.4, replacing 7.1.3 ) broke my system : after rebooting, when getting to the connection screen I believe, I’ve got no display / the screen is all black (but on).<br>\nI’ve tried switching from Displayport to HDMI, even to HDMI on my MB with no better result.</p>\n<p>I’ve tried booting to the previous version (which still works fine), cleaning the laster kernel, redoing the update : same result.</p>\n<p>What can I do to identify the problem ?</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2026-07-23T07:05:11.899Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 124, "reads": 29, "readers_count": 28, "score": 630.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 197473, "topic_slug": "latest-update-kernel-7-1-4-nvidia-4070-black-screen", "display_username": "Natha TERR", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 34675, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 0, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/latest-update-kernel-7-1-4-nvidia-4070-black-screen/197473/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 518957, "name": "Steve Flynn", "username": "anothermindbomb", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/anothermindbomb/{size}/56713_2.png", "created_at": "2026-07-23T11:49:18.170Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"njxt72\" data-display-name=\"Natha TERR\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"197473\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/n/3c6eb4/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Natha TERR:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I’ve tried booting to the previous version (which still works fine), cleaning the laster kernel, redoing the update : same result.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Does booting to an earlier kernel in Grub make any difference or does each kernel you have available to you present the same dead screen? It’s not obvious to me what you mean in this statement…</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2026-07-23T11:50:43.204Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 3, "reads": 24, "readers_count": 23, "score": 24.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 197473, "topic_slug": "latest-update-kernel-7-1-4-nvidia-4070-black-screen", "display_username": "Steve Flynn", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 22579, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/latest-update-kernel-7-1-4-nvidia-4070-black-screen/197473/2", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 518959, "name": "Steve Flynn", "username": "anothermindbomb", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/anothermindbomb/{size}/56713_2.png", "created_at": "2026-07-23T11:52:27.049Z", "cooked": "<p>Assuming you can boot something which gives you a screen, please post the last 15 or so lines from <code>/var/cache/akmods/nvidia/.last.log</code> as preformatted text.</p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2026-07-23T11:52:27.049Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 2, "reads": 24, "readers_count": 23, "score": 14.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 197473, "topic_slug": "latest-update-kernel-7-1-4-nvidia-4070-black-screen", "display_username": "Steve Flynn", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 22579, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/latest-update-kernel-7-1-4-nvidia-4070-black-screen/197473/3", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 518966, "name": "Natha TERR", "username": "njxt72", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/n/3c6eb4/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-07-23T12:06:54.318Z", "cooked": "<blockquote>\n<p>Does booting to an earlier kernel in Grub make any difference or does each kernel you have available to you present the same dead screen? It’s not obvious to me what you mean in this statement…</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Booting on the previous kernel works fine: I don’t have any display problems with it.</p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2026-07-23T12:06:54.318Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 5, "reads": 22, "readers_count": 21, "score": 34.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 197473, "topic_slug": "latest-update-kernel-7-1-4-nvidia-4070-black-screen", "display_username": "Natha TERR", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 22579, "username": "anothermindbomb", "name": "Steve Flynn", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/anothermindbomb/{size}/56713_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 34675, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 0, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/latest-update-kernel-7-1-4-nvidia-4070-black-screen/197473/4", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 518968, "name": "Steve Flynn", "username": "anothermindbomb", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/anothermindbomb/{size}/56713_2.png", "created_at": "2026-07-23T12:09:37.993Z", "cooked": "<p>Excellent - lets see what you have in .last.log from the previous build of the nvidia drivers for the knackered kernel.</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2026-07-23T12:09:37.993Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 4, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 21, "readers_count": 20, "score": 9.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 197473, "topic_slug": "latest-update-kernel-7-1-4-nvidia-4070-black-screen", "display_username": "Steve Flynn", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "reply_to_user": {"id": 34675, "username": "njxt72", "name": "Natha TERR", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/n/3c6eb4/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 22579, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/latest-update-kernel-7-1-4-nvidia-4070-black-screen/197473/5", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 518976, "name": "Natha TERR", "username": "njxt72", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/n/3c6eb4/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-07-23T12:50:37.533Z", "cooked": "<p>Nevermind, I found the problem.<br>\nThere was no log for the latest Nvidia driver and the latest kernel in <code>/var/cache/akmods/nvidia/</code><br>\nSo, I tried to recompile (?) it with sudo akmods --force but akmods was not available anymore (can’t figure out why though)!<br>\nSo did a <code>sudo dnf install akmod-nvidia</code><br>\nThen  <code>sudo akmods --force</code><br>\nAnd after rebooting, everything was ok.<br>\nLesson learned.<br>\nThanks for leading me on the right path and learning the existence of <code>/var/cache/akmods/nvidia/</code></p>", "post_number": 6, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2026-07-23T12:51:09.887Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 5, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 2, "reads": 21, "readers_count": 20, "score": 34.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 197473, "topic_slug": "latest-update-kernel-7-1-4-nvidia-4070-black-screen", "display_username": "Natha TERR", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 22579, "username": "anothermindbomb", "name": "Steve Flynn", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/anothermindbomb/{size}/56713_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 34675, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 0, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/latest-update-kernel-7-1-4-nvidia-4070-black-screen/197473/6", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "bluethumb", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": true, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 518988, "name": "Mark", "username": "anotheruser", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/anotheruser/{size}/57144_2.png", "created_at": "2026-07-23T14:24:47.694Z", "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"njxt72\" data-display-name=\"Natha TERR\" data-post=\"6\" data-topic=\"197473\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/n/3c6eb4/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Natha TERR:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>So, I tried to recompile (?) it with sudo akmods --force but akmods was not available anymore (can’t figure out why though)!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Did you remove the latest kernel-devel at some point?</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\"># rpm -qa kernel-devel\nkernel-devel-7.0.14-201.fc44.x86_64\nkernel-devel-7.1.2-201.fc44.x86_64\nkernel-devel-7.1.3-201.fc44.x86_64\nkernel-devel-7.1.4-202.fc44.x86_64\nkernel-devel-7.1.4-204.fc44.x86_64\n\n# dnf remove kernel-devel-7.1.4-204.fc44.x86_64 --assumeno \nPackage                    Arch    Version                    Repository           Size\nRemoving:\n kernel-devel              x86_64  0:7.1.4-204.fc44           updates          87.9 MiB\nRemoving dependent packages:\n akmod-nvidia              x86_64  3:610.43.03-1.fc44         @commandline     99.2 KiB\n akmods                    noarch  0:0.6.2-9.fc44             fedora           66.0 KiB\nRemoving unused dependencies:\n kernel-devel-matched      x86_64  0:7.1.4-204.fc44           updates           0.0   B\n\nTransaction Summary:\n Removing:           4 packages\n\n# dnf remove kernel-devel-7.1.4-202.fc44.x86_64 --assumeno \nPackage                    Arch    Version                     Repository          Size\nRemoving:\n kernel-devel              x86_64  0:7.1.4-202.fc44            updates         87.9 MiB\n\nTransaction Summary:\n Removing:           1 package\n</code></pre>", "post_number": 7, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 9, "updated_at": "2026-07-23T14:24:47.694Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 6, "quote_count": 1, "incoming_link_count": 2, "reads": 18, "readers_count": 17, "score": 18.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 197473, "topic_slug": "latest-update-kernel-7-1-4-nvidia-4070-black-screen", "display_username": "Mark", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "reply_to_user": {"id": 34675, "username": "njxt72", "name": "Natha TERR", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/n/3c6eb4/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 13117, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 3, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/latest-update-kernel-7-1-4-nvidia-4070-black-screen/197473/7", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_rea